(3395242, 471291, 22301, '<td valign="top">this is a great real moment, unlike many I have seen this challenge. BTW if there actors or friends kudos for a job well done :)</td>', 'this is a great real moment, unlike many I have seen this challenge. BTW if there actors or friends kudos for a job well done :)', '2007-02-22 19:53:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(3395258, 470961, 22301, '<td valign="top">The background I find alittle distracting and abit noisy, you could try a couple of things. One would be in the set up and have a few more feet between your subjects and the background this will put less light on the background and will be naturally darker, and if you use a shallow DoF you will not notice the wrinkles in the background. Second thing you can do if you don''t have more room is if you are working with curves take the slider where the shadows begin in the corner and slide it towards the middle the background will soom go dark, you can then click somehwere on the skin and it should show you where it is on the line and you can lighten that area.</td>', 'The background I find alittle distracting and abit noisy, you could try a couple of things. One would be in the set up and have a few more feet between your subjects and the background this will put less light on the background and will be naturally darker, and if you use a shallow DoF you will not notice the wrinkles in the background. Second thing you can do if you don''t have more room is if you are working with curves take the slider where the shadows begin in the corner and slide it towards the middle the background will soom go dark, you can then click somehwere on the skin and it should show you where it is on the line and you can lighten that area.', '2007-02-22 20:03:36.000000', NULL, 1),
