(4359735, 472573, 78062, '<td valign="top">I love the DOF here how it drags your eye  to the bottom of the frame but the out of focus bird adds a little interest point to the background. I do feel that it could benefit from a bit more processing though, maybe using the levels command and shifting the slider on the right into the middle a bit more to brighten the whole thing up a shade. You caught the moment well but as someone else mentioned, it''s a shame the resize killed the details in the facial expressions.<br/> <br/>For one, I usually smart sharpen after the resize on a very low setting just to align the pixels a bit more and add a little touch of contrast.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps :)</td>', 'I love the DOF here how it drags your eye  to the bottom of the frame but the out of focus bird adds a little interest point to the background. I do feel that it could benefit from a bit more processing though, maybe using the levels command and shifting the slider on the right into the middle a bit more to brighten the whole thing up a shade. You caught the moment well but as someone else mentioned, it''s a shame the resize killed the details in the facial expressions. For one, I usually smart sharpen after the resize on a very low setting just to align the pixels a bit more and add a little touch of contrast. Hope this helps :)', '2008-01-04 08:24:39.000000', NULL, 0),
